<title>INDIA: Indian gold eases, silver ends steady.</title>
<headline>Indian gold eases, silver ends steady.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold prices eased on Wednesday but silver was steady in quiet listless trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices of gold biscuit (116.50 grammes) fell 50 rupees to 60,250 per piece after losing 100 rupees on Tuesday. It was up 400 rupees on Monday.</p>
<p>Activity was light in silver.  </p>
